    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101318" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύρροος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύρρους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>flowing
				together, confluent</i>, Ti. 
				Locr.
			<i><span class="en">
				101e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				104a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίμνη τῇ θαλάττῃ ς</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				10.10.12
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.40.9
			</span></i>: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.1.2
			</span></i>, al.; of an isthmus, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύρρουν ποτὲ
				ὑπάρξαντα</span>, i.e. once covered by the seas, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.2.32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
